<article class="qj-origin"><header class="qj-opening"><span class="qj-kicker">Our Story / Jeff & Vanessa</span><h1>A place to grow into.<br><em>A life to enjoy now.</em></h1><p>We’re building toward our retirement Happy Place. We’re not waiting until someday to start living it.</p></header><div class="qj-origin-pair"><figure>{{ {mediaId:"media-2747fb85f929",alt:"Jeff and Vanessa together at the cabin",loading:"eager",fetchpriority:"high"} | mediaImage | safe }}<figcaption>The two of us behind Quiet Backyard Living.</figcaption></figure><div><span class="qj-kicker">We’re Jeff and Vanessa</span><h2>Not perfect.<br><em>Not fancy. Just ours.</em></h2><p>In 2022, we were looking for something quieter. The little property we found was rough, unfinished, and full of things to figure out. But underneath all that, we could see a place to breathe.</p><p>The first weekends weren’t comfortable in any polished way. We kept coming back, bringing what we needed, learning the next job, and imagining what the place could become.</p><a class="qj-text-link" href="/our-journey/chapters/chapter-01">Read the beginning, rough edges and all <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
<div class="qj-origin-reading"><section><h2>What Happy Place means to us.</h2><p>Some food from the garden. Useful things made by hand. Wildlife that starts to feel familiar. Somewhere to work, learn, sit outside, and enjoy being here together.</p><p>The cabin has needed more work than we expected. The city beds have struggled while we were away. We’ve built things we love, and things we’ve wanted to walk away from for a while. Those parts belong in the story too.</p></section><section><h2>One life. Two places.</h2><p>Home, with the gardens and the projects between trips. The Gladwin cabin, with its own work, wildlife and quieter moments. Both are part of the life we’re building toward—not separate versions of us.</p><a class="qj-text-link" href="/pages/our-place">A little more about the place <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section><section><h2>Then we started sharing it.</h2><p>Over the winter before the 2026 season, little birdhouse builds became Vanessa’s Christmas Sip & Build, gifts, and ideas for more wildlife projects. The idea for this website followed: a place to share the projects, setbacks, critters and small moments along the way.</p><a class="qj-text-link" href="/our-journey/chapters/chapter-24">The winter that became a chapter <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section><section><h2>The place is the setting.<br><em>The life is the point.</em></h2><p>We’re still learning and still making plans. You’re welcome to follow along—or take a useful idea back to a place of your own.</p><div class="qj-origin-actions"><a class="qj-button" href="/our-journey/chapters/chapter-01">Start at Chapter One <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="qj-text-link" href="{{ journey.book.latest.route }}">Read the latest chapter <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section></div></article>
